cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "fuzzy_llm_matcher: Reliable fuzzy matching with optional LLM review and geospatial support"
version: 0.2.0-alpha
date-released: 2026-08-06
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21803695
authors:
  - family-names: "Mohseni Aref"
    given-names: "Mohammad"
    affiliation: "University of Potsdam"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/mohseniaref/fuzzy_llm_matcher"
url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21803695"
abstract: >
  fuzzy_llm_matcher is a Python library for reliable fuzzy matching of noisy
  tabular and geospatial data. It combines deterministic string similarity,
  score-margin based confidence estimation, optional LLM review for ambiguous
  cases, and a full geospatial matching pipeline including spatial blocking,
  geo-distance scoring, coordinate-uncertainty-aware matching, geometry
  similarity scores (Hausdorff, Fréchet, IoU), transliteration, phonetic
  scoring, hexagonal grid blocking, and tile basemap visualisation.
keywords:
  - fuzzy matching
  - record linkage
  - entity resolution
  - deduplication
  - large language models
  - geospatial
  - gis
  - toponym
  - place names
  - transliteration
  - phonetic matching
  - spatial blocking
  - hexagonal grid
  - admin boundaries
